The potential vulnerability is related to file upload handling, specifically an Unrestricted File Upload vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application allows users to upload files without adequately validating the file type or content. In the context of the provided API for converting zip files into text files, if the application does not enforce strict checks on the uploaded zip files, it could lead to the execution of malicious files or scripts contained within the zip. This could compromise the server's security, allowing attackers to execute arbitrary code or access sensitive data, as the application may inadvertently process harmful files that are not properly filtered or restricted.

